{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage","id":1559726,"title":"A problem with Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-03T10:31:58-07:00","id":1559726,"title":"A problem with Mage?","content":"When the game first came out in the 1990s, the Nine Spheres were meant to be analogous to the nine planets, but now there are only eight planets. What should an ST do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T12:02:57-07:00","id":1559729,"title":"","content":"Options I can think of:<br /> <br /> 1 - Ignore the new definition (the modern definition has problems)<br /> <br /> 2 - The 3 rule definition (orbits the sun, big enough to be spherical, big enough to clear its orbit) technically would include the moon. So you could count the moon as a planet. Though\u2026 now that I think of it, wasn\u2019t Mage doing that already?<br /> <br /> 3 - Put in another planet that hasn\u2019t been found yet.<br /> <br /> What storyline do you have planned where this connection is relevant? That might give some indication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T12:05:30-07:00","id":1559730,"title":"","content":"I think I like the option that Pluto, even if it\u2019s technically not big enough to qualify as a planet, nonetheless has sufficient Entropy Resonance to be connected to that Sphere. But thank you so much for your ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T12:40:40-07:00","id":1559731,"title":"","content":"I always went with &quot;the reason why Pluto was declassified was because the technocrats are deathly afraid of the shard realm of entropy and since they can't police it's entrance like Senex, they hoped that by rejecting it as a planet, the consensus effect might either weaken the shard realms power, or hopefully close it's doors entirely&quot;<br /> <br /> Now of course, there have been many talks recently of a &quot;planet X&quot;. I go with the idea that the gambit of the technocracy partially worked, Pluto's entrance to the realm is mostly closed. But Entropy won't be denied so it began to manifest another way. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T12:59:45-07:00","id":1559732,"title":"","content":"Given the setup of Mage... the reclassification of Pluto could be an actual Technocratic scheme to depower the Tradition stronghold there (or a number of other Future Fates that you could tie in like trying to put up a firewall against Threat Null).<br /> <br /> That said, I think you have your initial premise a bit backwards. The Nine Spheres were not picked from traditional astrology because most traditional astrologies only have 7 celestial bodies besides Earth: the Sun, the Moon, and the five visible planets (Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn). Though some older versions thought Venus was two different planets. The Mage creators retrofit the accepted nine planets of the time back into the cosmology of Mage. Keep in mind that Pluto wasn't even officially discovered until 1930 because it's that hard to detect (though there was some evidence of it existing before that to cause scientists to look for it). For everyone that's yapping about Mage here, Pluto has always been part of our known world. A hundred years ago nobody would have known about some planet named Pluto. <br /> <br /> The reclassification of Pluto is actually easier on Mage as a game because instead of suborning any major occurrence of a set of nine as something with Sphere correspondences regardless of how well that meshes with the real world inspirations for the various Mage groups, you can play a 7 body astrologer Mage that doesn't have to care about how the discovery of lots of other things floating around in space well after their belief systems were formalized get labelled by scientists. Even if that's a different problem with integrating various metaplot stuff, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T14:30:47-07:00","id":1559735,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms and Nyreme get my vote. Most real world astrologers don't really keep up with astronomy. Why would a centuries old Hermetic or Verbena? Tell the local equivalent of Granny Weatherwax or Catweazle about the latest discoveries in extrasolar astronomy and they might smile and ask you to pass the sugar. <br /> <br /> The Chakravanti have better to do than worry about what the Technocracy tells school children about Pluto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T14:49:29-07:00","id":1559736,"title":"","content":"I would say it depends a bit. In the New Age style astrology, there tends to be a love of adding in the dwarf planets as an additional layer of astrology (you can find astrology charts that include brand new correspondences for Ceres, Eris, and so on).<br /> <br /> I mean, there's some decent Mage story fodder for debates between the older versions/reconstruction style astrologers, and the New Age style ones. It's hard to put a real world rating on what &quot;most&quot; do, because I'm not aware of anyone that seriously collects data on that. But there are certainly old school mages that want to do things the way things were done centuries ago, and others that want to update to keep more in-line with Consensus if only because they're younger and just disregarding centuries of discoveries they grew up with feels wrong.<br /> <br /> I also think how much the Traditions should or would care about these things would come down a lot to how much they perceive it as an active effort of the Union, or just a side effect of the Technocrats' manipulations of Sleeper science. If enough Tradition (or Disparate) mages are convinced the Technocracy is up to something, they're going to care simply because you can't really just ignore that. It might not be because what school kids are taught to call Pluto, but because whatever the reason to start pushing that is good for the Union and thus bad for everyone else in the world of mages.<br /> <br /> Of course, if it's not really a plot and just Sleeper science going to the logical conclusions of things the Technocrats set in motion decades ago, then it's more likely for most mages to not find a reason to put energy into it over all of the other things going on to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T15:14:09-07:00","id":1559737,"title":"","content":"I think the more interesting discovery (at least for Traditions and Crafts) is that Pluto-Charon behaves more like a binary system with the barycenter outside of Pluto, and what that means in correspondece to the Shard Realm and/or the Sphere. As the others have mentioned, Magick metaphysics tend to ignore mundane reclassifications as long as the concept stays intact- ie, Pluto still works as the 'conceptual expression' of Entropy even if it is now classified as a dwarf planet.<br /> <br /> The duality of Pluto-Charon is more interesting however because it expands this concept to a 'twin' situation. There was probably some discussion among the Traditions whether it explains the entwinement of Fate and Entropy in the Sphere, or if it represents two different aspects of Entropy, or the same but split in two..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T16:19:32-07:00","id":1559738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559737#post1559737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the more interesting discovery (at least for Traditions and Crafts) is that Pluto-Charon behaves more like a binary system with the barycenter outside of Pluto, and what that means in correspondece to the Shard Realm and/or the Sphere. As the others have mentioned, Magick metaphysics tend to ignore mundane reclassifications as long as the concept stays intact- ie, Pluto still works as the 'conceptual expression' of Entropy even if it is now classified as a dwarf planet.<br /> <br /> The duality of Pluto-Charon is more interesting however because it expands this concept to a 'twin' situation. There was probably some discussion among the Traditions whether it explains the entwinement of Fate and Entropy in the Sphere, or if it represents two different aspects of Entropy, or the same but split in two..</div> </div> </div> </div>Very creative. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T17:39:29-07:00","id":1559742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559737#post1559737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the more interesting discovery (at least for Traditions and Crafts) is that Pluto-Charon behaves more like a binary system with the barycenter outside of Pluto, and what that means in correspondece to the Shard Realm and/or the Sphere. As the others have mentioned, Magick metaphysics tend to ignore mundane reclassifications as long as the concept stays intact- ie, Pluto still works as the 'conceptual expression' of Entropy even if it is now classified as a dwarf planet.<br /> <br /> The duality of Pluto-Charon is more interesting however because it expands this concept to a 'twin' situation. There was probably some discussion among the Traditions whether it explains the entwinement of Fate and Entropy in the Sphere, or if it represents two different aspects of Entropy, or the same but split in two..</div> </div> </div> </div>Logged in just to say this, and found someone already suggested it, so good work. There is some theories to Eris and its moon also being a binary system, so perhaps the Tenth Sphere is tied to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T15:08:21-07:00","id":1559775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage#post1559726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the game first came out in the 1990s, the Nine Spheres were meant to be analogous to the nine planets, but now there are only eight planets. What should an ST do?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bigger problem is, for the longest time, there was only six-planets; so ancient-mages only had six-spheres?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T18:48:21-07:00","id":1559780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559775#post1559775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bigger problem is, for the longest time, there was only six-planets; so ancient-mages only had six-spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually didn\u2019t have spheres until the Renaissance. In ancient times they used Pillars. But you\u2019re right, for a few centuries there were nine Spheres and only six planets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T04:33:12-07:00","id":1559783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559737#post1559737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the more interesting discovery (at least for Traditions and Crafts) is that Pluto-Charon behaves more like a binary system with the barycenter outside of Pluto, and what that means in correspondece to the Shard Realm and/or the Sphere. As the others have mentioned, Magick metaphysics tend to ignore mundane reclassifications as long as the concept stays intact- ie, Pluto still works as the 'conceptual expression' of Entropy even if it is now classified as a dwarf planet.<br /> <br /> The duality of Pluto-Charon is more interesting however because it expands this concept to a 'twin' situation. There was probably some discussion among the Traditions whether it explains the entwinement of Fate and Entropy in the Sphere, or if it represents two different aspects of Entropy, or the same but split in two..</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!<br /> <br /> I was going to suggest the duality of Hades/Persephone or Pluto/Persopine. This based on the reason Pluto was declassified because it does not maintain its own orbit and is effected by its moon. The two body &quot;planet&quot; and its interesting possibilities for Mage discussions about the seemingly dual nature of Entropy of death and fate or chance is the big win for players. Just the idea that Pluto is the farthest planet allows conjecture about whether we are all bound within their orbit.<br /> <br /> Was very happy to see you beat me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T04:33:19-07:00","id":1559815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559780#post1559780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They actually didn\u2019t have spheres until the Renaissance. In ancient times they used Pillars. But you\u2019re right, for a few centuries there were nine Spheres and only six planets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Six planets <i>known to mortals</i>. You could also say that having 9 spheres was a giveaway that there must be more planets to find, just as Neptune having a wonky orbit led astronomers to look for Pluto. Even if someone travelled to the associated Realm, and new for sure the planet must exist somewhere, you still couldn't conclusively spot them until astronomy tools improved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T07:15:10-07:00","id":1559819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559815#post1559815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Six planets <i>known to mortals</i>. You could also say that having 9 spheres was a giveaway that there must be more planets to find, just as Neptune having a wonky orbit led astronomers to look for Pluto. Even if someone travelled to the associated Realm, and new for sure the planet must exist somewhere, you still couldn't conclusively spot them until astronomy tools improved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Mage is vague on how much a part of reality the Spheres actually are (likely because the authors had different views). They can range anywhere from a a language convention that's existed long enough its started showing up in umbral realms, to one of many mythic threads that run through reality, to foundational structures built into reality. Not only that, but even if the Spheres have more weight than just convention, mages wouldn't know that automatically. They couldn't use their terminology to deduce the existence of the Shard realms. They'd have to know of the Shard realms first before they could tell the Spheres pointed to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T13:13:07-07:00","id":1559825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559775#post1559775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bigger problem is, for the longest time, there was only six-planets; so ancient-mages only had six-spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div>5 planets originally (the wandering stars) earth was not classified as a planet because it doesn't look like a star. The Moon and sun also didn't count...<br /> <br /> Maybe the odd comet here and there would be included, if they could find one. But I think the theory that the planets were inscribed in the celestial spheres was invented much later (Renaissance-ish?)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T15:52:07-07:00","id":1559996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559729#post1559729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Options I can think of:<br /> <br /> 1 - Ignore the new definition (the modern definition has problems)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say ignore it.<br /> <br /> Science is a lie, created by the Technocracy to stifle humanity's limitless potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T16:33:41-07:00","id":1559998,"title":"","content":"Or... not double down on the 1e anti-science stuff because that was removed from the game for a ton of good reasons. And the most important reason: the game is more fun when it approaches science with more nuance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T20:33:43-07:00","id":1560000,"title":"","content":"Given how many people stubbornly refuse to accept Pluto getting downgraded, if it WAS a Technocrat plot, it doesn't seem to have worked as well as they'd hoped.<br /> <br /> If anything, it kind of underscores how arbitrary the scientific classification of &quot;Planet&quot; is. Which might somewhat undermine the Technocratic paradigm of &quot;Science is based on absolutely objective, rules-based facts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T21:15:34-07:00","id":1560004,"title":"","content":"How many people actually object though (esp. as there are now people in college/university who were born after the reclassification happened)? How many people even know the basic science on why the decision was made, let alone the more utility base cladistic argument for it?<br /> <br /> There are still flat-earthers around. There are people that reject that evolution is a thing (and mistake the observed fact of evolution and the theory of evolution as the same thing instead of a thing we see and the way we explain why it happens the way it happens). As I see it much like those two groups, the &quot;Pluto is a true planet&quot; crowd has been sufficiently stereotyped and pushed to the fringes of mainstream thought that it would seem well within the Technocrat's tolerances for the basic human inclination towards anti-intellectualism and beliefs that seem to get clung to stemming from that.<br /> <br /> This also leads into something I didn't think is a fair representation. The Technocrats do no hold science itself as their paradigm (that's basically impossible), nor is that how anyone (esp. the Technocracy) would define science. A key element to real world science that is also a key point of utility for the Union to pursue its goals, is that science changes as we expand and refine our knowledge of the universe. The Technocracy doesn't want an overly rigid science with no self-correcting mechanisms. Those major shifts in scientific consensus are what lets them drive the Time Table forward as new expansions of scientific understanding means Sleepers are ready to have more enlightened hyper-science moved into normal Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T02:01:18-07:00","id":1560015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560000#post1560000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, it kind of underscores how arbitrary the scientific classification of &quot;Planet&quot; is. Which might somewhat undermine the Technocratic paradigm of &quot;Science is based on absolutely objective, rules-based facts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classifications are just a tool to categorize data to make it easier to work with. As such, they are an emergent result of facts, not fact by themselves. They are a perspective. The biological Taxon gets revised constantly as science produces new results, the Standard Model is the best working (but by no means only) perspective on particle physics we have.<br /> <br /> From a Mage's point of view, their paradigm determines which system of classification they use, but they understand that different paradigms work and produce results even if it is completely alien to their own. The Technocracy does, too - on a fundamental level, the disagreement between Union and Traditions is the same as between individual branches within both societies. The difference is just that the Traditions use mysticism and the Technocrats use science as a language to express their respective perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T06:41:47-07:00","id":1560024,"title":"","content":"Oh well the memory trick still runs. <br /> <br /> Mary's violet eyes make John stay up nights.<br /> <br /> Or maybe..<br /> <br /> Mark's violet eyes make Joan stay up nights. <br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> Mary's violet eyes make Joan stay up nights. <br /> <br /> Or even...<br /> <br /> Mark's violet eyes make John stay up nights. <br /> <br /> Whatever works for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T05:13:38-07:00","id":1560089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560000#post1560000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how many people stubbornly refuse to accept Pluto getting downgraded, if it WAS a Technocrat plot, it doesn't seem to have worked as well as they'd hoped.<br /> <br /> If anything, it kind of underscores how arbitrary the scientific classification of &quot;Planet&quot; is. Which might somewhat undermine the Technocratic paradigm of &quot;Science is based on absolutely objective, rules-based facts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between Pluto, the Moon Landing, and Threat Null, I'm getting the sense that the Technocracy doesn't have the best track record when it comes to space exploration.<br /> <br /> Which serves them right, when those fuckers keep telling us that cryo stasis pods, and FTL travel are impossible.<br /> <br /> The Sons of Ether are probably laughing all the way to Saturn!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T05:18:50-07:00","id":1560090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560004#post1560004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people actually object though (esp. as there are now people in college/university who were born after the reclassification happened)? How many people even know the basic science on why the decision was made, let alone the more utility base cladistic argument for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to comment on flat earthers, but you beat me to it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T05:36:32-07:00","id":1560091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559998#post1559998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or... not double down on the 1e anti-science stuff because that was removed from the game for a ton of good reasons. And the most important reason: the game is more fun when it approaches science with more nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the game is more fun when it approaches science from the Sons of Ether, or the Virtual Adepts paradigm. You can have flying cars, immersive VR implants, or travel across solar systems in the span of a few weeks (as opposed to centuries).<br /> <br /> <br /> The Technocracy want to sterilize everything. They want to cut out, stomp and burn everything fantastic about the world.<br /> <br /> All that talk about how they made the world a better place for humans? Complete bullshit.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, we invented modern medicine, instead of relying on superstitious remedies.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Bitch, they're only superstitious, because you convinced the world that was the case!</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Well our medicine is easier to access, than hiring some wizard or faith healer to treat you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>My medical bills say otherwise!!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Well, at least there are no kaiju wandering into human cities and destroying our civilization.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Yeah, because inventing a bomb that could do the job for them, and render the surrounding landscape uninhabitable for hundreds of years was such a great alternative!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T18:13:16-07:00","id":1560103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560091#post1560091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the game is more fun when it approaches science from the Sons of Ether, or the Virtual Adepts paradigm. You can have flying cars, immersive VR implants, or travel across solar systems in the span of a few weeks (as opposed to centuries).</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, the whole you post big hyperbolic nonsense thing doesn't to work for productive conversations between the two of us.<br /> <br /> So I'm just going to point out this: you're contradicting yourself. Science cannot be a lie created by the Technocracy (somehow, centuries after the scientific method was first developed), and something that technomages like the Etherites and VAs do as well. Either it's a lie that kills fantasy, or it's more nuanced. It can't be both. It can be a tool that functions as its users desire, but that means it isn't a lie, it's just how the Technocrats use it that's wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T21:26:02-07:00","id":1560107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560103#post1560103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, the whole you post big hyperbolic nonsense thing doesn't to work for productive conversations between the two of us.<br /> <br /> So I'm just going to point out this: you're contradicting yourself. Science cannot be a lie created by the Technocracy (somehow, centuries after the scientific method was first developed), and something that technomages like the Etherites and VAs do as well. Either it's a lie that kills fantasy, or it's more nuanced. It can't be both. It can be a tool that functions as its users desire, but that means it isn't a lie, it's just how the Technocrats use it that's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the Etherites use can best be described as 'pseudo-science,' which those in the Technocracy have worked hard to convince the rest of the world &quot;is not real science.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The Etherites develop things that Consensus wishes could be scientifically possible, while the Technocracy develops things that could feasibly work.<br /> <br /> <br /> One has its roots grounded in the realm of science fiction, and the other is based on real life. At least the stuff that they allow the public to witness, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T02:17:47-07:00","id":1560109,"title":"","content":"What even is the point of that response? It's just a semantic shell game. Is there a particular reason why, &quot;Yeah, science as a lie in Mage isn't actually good because a more nuanced take that lets the SoE, VAs, and the hidden fatnastical sci-fi Technocrat stuff actually function as parts of game,&quot; isn't something you're willing to say over twisting your words into a Gordian Knot of mental gymnastics that still ends in the same point but without having to concede an inch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T02:57:52-07:00","id":1560110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560109#post1560109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What even is the point of that response? It's just a semantic shell game. Is there a particular reason why, &quot;Yeah, science as a lie in Mage isn't actually good because a more nuanced take that lets the SoE, VAs, and the hidden fatnastical sci-fi Technocrat stuff actually function as parts of game,&quot; isn't something you're willing to say over twisting your words into a Gordian Knot of mental gymnastics that still ends in the same point but without having to concede an inch?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is the same as my previous post.<br /> <br /> The game is fun when you present science through the lens of the Etherites. Don't get hung up on the scientific accuracy of how their inventions work, and instead just roll with it.<br /> <br /> If you present science through the lens of what the Technocracy wants you to believe, it becomes stale and boring. They're the kind of scientists who have to ruin your list of favorite super powers, by explaining to you why having them would actually suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T03:12:32-07:00","id":1560111,"title":"","content":"But fun Etherite science can't exist in a world where science is, &quot;...a lie, created by the Technocracy to stifle humanity's limitless potential.&quot; Which is what you called it. You didn't say Technocratic science is bad, you said all science is bad, and you beeen waffling about trying to not retract the all science is bad post. Pointing at the Etherites is a red herring because they're defectors from the Union, as are the VAs, which means their science would have to be based in the same lie if you stand by the comment that sparked the tangent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T04:23:22-07:00","id":1560117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560111#post1560111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But fun Etherite science can't exist in a world where science is, &quot;...a lie, created by the Technocracy to stifle humanity's limitless potential.&quot; Which is what you called it. You didn't say Technocratic science is bad, you said all science is bad, and you beeen waffling about trying to not retract the all science is bad post. Pointing at the Etherites is a red herring because they're defectors from the Union, as are the VAs, which means their science would have to be based in the same lie if you stand by the comment that sparked the tangent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. They defected precisely because their version of science went outside the boundaries of what the Technocracy deemed acceptable.<br /> <br /> The union actively sabotaged the Etherites projects, and assassinated someone the VA's felt very highly of, because they were afraid of what their research would ultimately lead to.<br /> <br /> As for the waffling, my stance is that using real world science (the kind espoused by the Technocracy) does, in fact, ruin the fantasy aspects.<br /> <br /> To further elaborate my comparison about the super powers:<br /> <br /> <br /> Etherites would invent some kind of super soldier drug that gives you the brute strength of 10,000 men. Thus endowing you with ability to bench press motor vehicles, or catch people falling out of skyscraper windows.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy would push up their glasses, and proceed to give you a seminar about how surface tension would cause those vehicles to rip apart, or how landing in your outstretched arms would feel like smashing into a steel girder at terminal velocity.<br /> <br /> <br /> To paraphrase the Etherites: <i>&quot;Science should make more things possible, not less.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T08:14:52-07:00","id":1560122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etherites would invent some kind of super soldier drug that gives you the brute strength of 10,000 men. Thus endowing you with ability to bench press motor vehicles, or catch people falling out of skyscraper windows.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy would push up their glasses, and proceed to give you a seminar about how surface tension would cause those vehicles to rip apart, or how landing in your outstretched arms would feel like smashing into a steel girder at terminal velocity.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase the Etherites: <i>&quot;Science should make more things possible, not less.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Etherites don't skimp on the details. That's Marauders. Marauders make reality function however they want, Etherites find creative solutions to the small problems reality posits to them.<br /> <br /> A Marauder expects &quot;the superman&quot; trick to work, so it does even when it shouldn't work.<br /> <br /> An Etherite that's realy into it would instead make a &quot;law of applied heroism&quot; that allows superheroes (which probably differ from regular heroes because of &quot;the presenthation&quot;) to catch people falling out of skyscraper windows ingnoring the details of innertia. And then complain about the Technocracy not including it on the Time Table for Terranorming.<br /> <br /> BOTH cases are probably using Forces, or some other Sphere that can alter that reality, rather than just the Strength Trait - the difference it's one of them <i>knows</i> he's doing something (even if he expresses it w/o the ooc terminology) <hr /><br /> Or you may want to argue about the advantages of &quot;cinematic realism&quot; on your Mage.<br /> <br /> There's some level of support for it, with the optional rule of mages soacking lethal and dodging explosions with lvl 1 magick - tho it's more &quot;Rambo punching trough glass&quot; than Golden Age superheroes<br /> <br /> But that has nothing to do with the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-20-2026, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T12:07:17-07:00","id":1560124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560117#post1560117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. You're wrong on this. Objectively and beyond any hope of posting words out of it. You have three basic options: acknowledge your mistake and try to learn from it to move forward, drop it and move on and maybe try to come up with a less obviously wrong take next time you get into one of these discussions, or keeping telling us how much you love showing off being wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the waffling, my stance is that using real world science (the kind espoused by the Technocracy) does, in fact, ruin the fantasy aspects. </div> </div> </div>On behalf of myself and all of my fellow real world scientists? Fuck off.<br /> <br /> You are too ignorant and/or ill-informed for this conversation. You don't know what science actually is, or even what it's like to try to be a scientist in the current state of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T14:37:48-07:00","id":1560128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560122#post1560122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Etherite that's realy into it would instead make a &quot;law of applied heroism&quot; that allows superheroes (which probably differ from regular heroes because of &quot;the presenthation&quot;) to catch people falling out of skyscraper windows ingnoring the details of innertia. And then complain about the Technocracy not including it on the Time Table for Terranorming.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the explanation of <i>&quot;Looney DNA&quot;</i> being what allows cartoon characters to recover from virtually anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Viltrumites being so powerful, because their bodies are composed of <i>&quot;Smart Atoms.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Fun, pseudo-science shit! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T14:43:26-07:00","id":1560129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560124#post1560124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On behalf of myself and all of my fellow real world scientists? Fuck off.<br /> <br /> You are too ignorant and/or ill-informed for this conversation. You don't know what science actually is, or even what it's like to try to be a scientist in the current state of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's real world scientists like yourself who say I'll never step foot on an alien planet, but my great, great, great, great grandchildren might possibly do so. If they survive the thousand year voyage through space.<br /> <br /> So, on behalf of all nine mystic traditions, You and your fellow scientists can fuck right off too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T16:31:25-07:00","id":1560132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560117#post1560117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To paraphrase the Etherites: <i>&quot;Science should make more things possible, not less.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560129#post1560129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's real world scientists like yourself who say I'll never step foot on an alien planet, but my great, great, great, great grandchildren might possibly do so. If they survive the thousand year voyage through space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Person, actual science takes the world as it is, at the same time as how doing so on a really deep and meticulous level does consistently find information that can be leveraged towards amazing results. The kind of thing that conducts experiments with prawns on treadmills and provides insight into biomechanics and ocean ecology.<br /> <br /> But actual physical limitations of the world aren't something that exists because some people are mean about it, and incredulity won't make them so.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T17:00:58-07:00","id":1560133,"title":"","content":"Also we don't get to say how our research gets used by wider society. Almost every scientific advancement entails technology that can be used for the betterment of humanity, or the detriment. You can't discover how to make a retro-viral cure for a genetic disorders without laying the groundwork for someone else to invent retro-viral poisons that harmfully edit the afflicted people's genes. FTL spaceships mean FTL kinetic planet killer weapons. If you can fling a spaceship across the void fast enough so that a 40 light-year trip takes four days? You can fire a tungsten WMD with enough energy to crack a rocky planet's crust open like breaking open an egg.<br /> <br /> Optimism about the advancement of science leading to getting closer and closer to a utopian world of endless discoveries is not about the science, it's about optimism in humans to figure out how to make sure the science is only used for the good things and not the bad things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T17:11:17-07:00","id":1560134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560132#post1560132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But actual physical limitations of the world aren't something that exists because some people are mean about it, and incredulity won't make them so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not delusional (enough) to think they do. I'm talking about from an in game perspective. The Technocracy has convinced the world that it operates in accordance to real world science and logic.<br /> <br /> Anything considered 'superstitious' or 'unrealistic' is only considered as such, because a bunch of technomancers told everybody that was the case, until they finally started believing it.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> The reason why I say science is a lie in Mage, is because reality is malleable, for those who have Awakened to the truth of the universe. How can you scientifically quantify, test, or explore something that changes its very laws and principles simply because you choose to believe that is how they operate?<br /> <br /> That, to me, sounds completely illogical; which is what science claims to be opposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T20:53:30-07:00","id":1560135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560133#post1560133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also we don't get to say how our research gets used by wider society. Almost every scientific advancement entails technology that can be used for the betterment of humanity, or the detriment. You can't discover how to make a retro-viral cure for a genetic disorders without laying the groundwork for someone else to invent retro-viral poisons that harmfully edit the afflicted people's genes. FTL spaceships mean FTL kinetic planet killer weapons. If you can fling a spaceship across the void fast enough so that a 40 light-year trip takes four days? You can fire a tungsten WMD with enough energy to crack a rocky planet's crust open like breaking open an egg.<br /> <br /> Optimism about the advancement of science leading to getting closer and closer to a utopian world of endless discoveries is not about the science, it's about optimism in humans to figure out how to make sure the science is only used for the good things and not the bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, when it is villainous, is not so because of abstract ideas of &quot;killing wonder&quot;. They're villainous because they marry scientific advancement to authoritarian systems, unjust hierarchies, and (especially in the 20th century) <i>White Supremacy</i>. And because they apply that &quot;join or go to Room 101&quot; mentality to their Mage enemies, usurping their autonomy &quot;for their own good&quot;.<br /> <br /> When the New World Order are evil, it's because they use their mastery of information, psychological, and social sciences for control. They're evil for the same reasons the CIA is evil, not because they believe in Psychology or because Q-Division likes to make gadgets that fit in your wristwatch. They CHOOSE to put a bomb in that wristwatch, rather than smartphone technology.<br /> <br /> When the Syndicate are evil, it's because they support and undergird exploitative and extractive business practices, and consolidate industries under increasingly smaller number of huge corporations. Economics ITSELF isn't evil, nor is a business degree. It's evil when you CHOOSE to make Profit the only goal worth pursuing, at the expense of everything else. <br /> <br /> When the Progenitors are evil, it's because some of them peddle illicit drugs, others replace your loved ones with clones, and others were largely okay with Modern Medicine being a commodity withheld for money. (That last bit, by the way, basically stopped being a problem everywhere in the world besides the US, because Universal Healthcare is a winning policy both Liberal and successful Authoritarian governments tend to agree on. It's only the US, with its for-profit healthcare system, where Progenitor work is withheld from the masses.).<br /> <br /> These are not problems inherent to Modern Science. They're problems of POLICY. Of the goals to which the Union applies their Sciences, and how the benefits (and detriments) of Scientific Advancement are distributed.<br /> <br /> The Revised era (including the post-2004 material) onwards is about using the fact that Control was lost (and became Threat Null) to divorce the Technocracy from its worst impulses. (Except the Syndicate, who keep on being Capitalists, and thus the worst). They can be the Science Heroes they want to be, no less than the Etherites or Virtual Adepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T21:41:25-07:00","id":1560138,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Keep it civil. Suspensions have been issued. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T16:56:32-07:00","id":1560917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560135#post1560135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^This.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, when it is villainous, is not so because of abstract ideas of &quot;killing wonder&quot;. They're villainous because they marry scientific advancement to authoritarian systems, unjust hierarchies, and (especially in the 20th century) <i>White Supremacy</i>. And because they apply that &quot;join or go to Room 101&quot; mentality to their Mage enemies, usurping their autonomy &quot;for their own good&quot;.<br /> <br /> When the New World Order are evil, it's because they use their mastery of information, psychological, and social sciences for control. They're evil for the same reasons the CIA is evil, not because they believe in Psychology or because Q-Division likes to make gadgets that fit in your wristwatch. They CHOOSE to put a bomb in that wristwatch, rather than smartphone technology.<br /> <br /> When the Syndicate are evil, it's because they support and undergird exploitative and extractive business practices, and consolidate industries under increasingly smaller number of huge corporations. Economics ITSELF isn't evil, nor is a business degree. It's evil when you CHOOSE to make Profit the only goal worth pursuing, at the expense of everything else.<br /> <br /> When the Progenitors are evil, it's because some of them peddle illicit drugs, others replace your loved ones with clones, and others were largely okay with Modern Medicine being a commodity withheld for money. (That last bit, by the way, basically stopped being a problem everywhere in the world besides the US, because Universal Healthcare is a winning policy both Liberal and successful Authoritarian governments tend to agree on. It's only the US, with its for-profit healthcare system, where Progenitor work is withheld from the masses.).<br /> <br /> These are not problems inherent to Modern Science. They're problems of POLICY. Of the goals to which the Union applies their Sciences, and how the benefits (and detriments) of Scientific Advancement are distributed.<br /> <br /> The Revised era (including the post-2004 material) onwards is about using the fact that Control was lost (and became Threat Null) to divorce the Technocracy from its worst impulses. (Except the Syndicate, who keep on being Capitalists, and thus the worst). They can be the Science Heroes they want to be, no less than the Etherites or Virtual Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Technocracy is still practically blood bound to the NWO, and the Precepts of Damian haven't really been changed even though Control has been cut off. They're still mandated to destroy every culture besides their own. <br /> <br /> And they do, in fact, &quot;kill wonder.&quot; The Etherite idea of the Wall of Troy is proof that you can do Science!!! while not being bound to reduce wonder in society. The Technocracy just aren't real scientists; after all, they hide discoveries that would upend their Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T00:05:01-07:00","id":1561068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560917#post1560917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Technocracy just aren't real scientists; after all, they hide discoveries that would upend their Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I'm fairly certain is grounds for somebody's research being discredited and getting its author kicked out of the scientific community.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Etherites are uploading videos on youtube about home made lightsabers, plasma rifles, and mech walkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T21:20:01-07:00","id":1561269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560128#post1560128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also the explanation of <i>&quot;Looney DNA&quot;</i> being what allows cartoon characters to recover from virtually anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Viltrumites being so powerful, because their bodies are composed of <i>&quot;Smart Atoms.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Fun, pseudo-science shit! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, somebody decided to go through this topic and downvote every post I made.<br /> <br /> Not sure why they chose to target this one, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T21:47:16-07:00","id":1561273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1559996#post1559996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science is a lie, created by the Technocracy to stifle humanity's limitless potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in 1st Edition and it's a bad thing in that edition.<br /> <br /> Through 2nd it was changing, and by the end we get rid of this idea.<br /> <br /> No Mage faction is made of scientists. None of them. They may defend the Scientific Method (and many on both sides do), but Awakened are by nature incapable of following it. Also the Technocracy has as much impossible crazy stuff as anyone else.<br /> <br /> Scientists in Mage are Sleepers and make actual research and discoveries without need of Mages. They do discover things the Union didn't expect, by the way.<br /> <br /> Consensus is a theory. While it exists in the sense of human belief partially shaping reality around, the extent and limits aren't really known, and there are several observations that don't fit current models.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's a Technocratic theory. While the Traditions know human belief has some power over reality, they never thought they could make science disappear.<br /> <br /> Reality has overall escaped the Union's control long ago anyway. Guide to the Technocracy did make it clear the Union was frantically trying to retake it while keeping a facade of absolute power.<br /> <br /> This only worsened since. They are no more in control of reality than the Traditions now, even if they have more resources and connections. The world isn't as it is because the Union make it so. The world just is.<br /> <br /> You'll find more about this in M20 reading about Earthly Foundations and other aspects of Reality Zones. But the gist of it? Science is real and doesn't need meddling Awakened to work perfectly fine, give or take Reality Zones <b><i>considerably limited </i></b>effects.<br /> <br /> Pluto's place in both reality and the game is an almost irrelevant matter. The classification thing is just a convenience for research, as is any taxonomy. In Mage the Shard Realms are just a theory thing, not the base for the Spheres or something, whatever happens to them has no impact whatsoever on anything but, well, them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T22:12:21-07:00","id":1561275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561273#post1561273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocracy has as much impossible crazy stuff as anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they don't flash it around in public. Either because the NWO wants to hoard all the best toys for themselves, or because <i>&quot;the masses aren't ready to accept it yet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561273#post1561273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consensus is a theory. While it exists in the sense of human belief partially shaping reality around, the extent and limits aren't really known, and there are several observations that don't fit current models.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's a Technocratic theory. While the Traditions know human belief has some power over reality, they never thought they could make science disappear.<br /> <br /> Reality has overall escaped the Union's control long ago anyway. Guide to the Technocracy did make it clear the Union was frantically trying to retake it while keeping a facade of absolute power.<br /> <br /> This only worsened since. They are no more in control of reality than the Traditions now, even if they have more resources and connections. The world isn't as it is because the Union make it so. The world just is.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's something I just can't accept, or wrap my head around. Consensus has to be true, as there's no other explanation for why the Traditions would have fallen into decline, while the Technocracy rose to power.<br /> <br /> It had to be the result of a paradigm shift in humanity's collective viewpoint. Nothing else makes sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561273#post1561273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You'll find more about this in M20 reading about Earthly Foundations and other aspects of Reality Zones. But the gist of it? Science is real and doesn't need meddling Awakened to work perfectly fine, give or take Reality Zones <b><i>considerably limited </i></b>effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, then why are the Technocracy and the Traditions fighting tooth and nail to seize control of the narrative and convince people to accept their way of seeing things?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T22:56:21-07:00","id":1561278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561275#post1561275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but they don't flash it around in public. Either because the NWO wants to hoard all the best toys for themselves, or because <i>&quot;the masses aren't ready to accept it yet.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is irrelevant to the matter. The Union's plan is one thing, their beliefs are another. They don't reveal things partly because they have a strategic decision about the matter, partly for the same reason the Traditions do the same: Paradox hurts.<br /> <br /> But what they believe is crazy shit like lab-built flying monkeys and the Terminator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561275#post1561275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that's something I just can't accept, or wrap my head around. Consensus has to be true, as there's no other explanation for why the Traditions would have fallen into decline, while the Technocracy rose to power.<br /> <br /> It had to be the result of a paradigm shift in humanity's collective viewpoint. Nothing else makes sense.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know every other possible explanation to say that?<br /> <br /> Simplest explanation possible: not everything is Mages.<br /> <br /> Traditions and Technocracy aren't the only Mages around to begin with, and Mages aren't the only (or main) force in the universe.<br /> <br /> If the Consensus is real, it's still coming from the masses of Sleepers and not from Mages, so the Union may just have overestimated how much it was their work rather than humanity doing it by itself and the Order of Reason just got lucky.<br /> <br /> But if it isn't... Something else is happening to reality and Mages blundered by thinking they're so important while the actual problem is out there. Not a terribly hard concept, really, the idea that reality is its own thing and things may happen because of something else.<br /> <br /> As for evidence:<br /> <br /> - Paradox, Consensus and Backlashes are NOT constant forces in the setting. The rules of reality are changing with time since way before there was an Order of Reason. This is not just rules of the game, but in-lore changes in reality itself and how it reacts to magic, that Mages felt and wrote about. At least 4 changes have been recorded, for a total of 5 eras so to speak.<br /> <br /> - the masses are demonstrably superstitious, religious, averse to the scientific method even when embracing scientific discoveries and full of magical thinking. There was no reason for the Consensus to follow a scientific Paradigm when the reality is that most people think bad things happen because their gods are angry.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that if reality is shaped by human belief, then the most powerful countries in the world are China and India, since they each have more people than the whole of Europe and North America combined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561275#post1561275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> If that's the case, then why are the Technocracy and the Traditions fighting tooth and nail to seize control of the narrative and convince people to accept their way of seeing things?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they have lots of reasons to, including that the Consensus is an important Technocratic theory, which means they thought it was real anyway, it so happens it isn't the way they thought.<br /> <br /> Social control and Reality Zones are still real reasons to fight, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T00:05:07-07:00","id":1561282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561278#post1561278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know every other possible explanation to say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternative is that we're following Shadowrun Rules, where the power of magic is cyclical in nature; waxing in one age, and waning in the next.<br /> <br /> But if that is the case, then it doesn't account for how the traditions are still able to perform their feats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561278#post1561278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simplest explanation possible: not everything is Mages.<br /> <br /> Traditions and Technocracy aren't the only Mages around to begin with, and Mages aren't the only (or main) force in the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already saw another discussion about this kind of stuff in a different thread, where the argument was about how all the different splats clash with and contradict each other.<br /> <br /> For the sake of convenience, I'm going with the assumption that as this is a mage related thread, we are only using mage related subject matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561278#post1561278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Consensus is real, it's still coming from the masses of Sleepers and not from Mages, so the Union may just have overestimated how much it was their work rather than humanity doing it by itself and the Order of Reason just got lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, however...<br /> <br /> 1 - Technocrats are mages, regardless of how much they deny it.<br /> <br /> \u200b2 - Technocrats have spent centuries shaping the Sleeper's perception of reality, and by extension shaping Consensus.<br /> <br /> The fact they eventually lost control of the situation does not change the fact that the world as we currently understand it today was shaped by the Technocracy manipulating our world view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561278#post1561278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget that if reality is shaped by human belief, then the most powerful countries in the world are China and India, since they each have more people than the whole of Europe and North America combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you haven't heard of the <i>&quot;Let it Rot&quot;</i> movement, where China's youth are opting out of the work environment, and deliberately allowing the country to collapse around them?<br /> <br /> Also, didn't the CCP enforce atheism on a national level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:44:02-07:00","id":1561292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561282#post1561282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, didn't the CCP enforce atheism on a national level?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they did in the Mao era, but Chinese religion was too entrenched, and subsequent leaders gave it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:46:13-07:00","id":1561293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1560133#post1560133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FTL spaceships mean FTL kinetic planet killer weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the FTL method used. Wormholes for example wouldn't be able to create kinetic planet killer weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:56:24-07:00","id":1561294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561292#post1561292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe they did in the Mao era, but Chinese religion was too entrenched, and subsequent leaders gave it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just checking, because I remember something about them creating a law where Tibetan monks needed the government's permission to reincarnate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which, hilariously, sounds like something the Celestial Bureaucracy might come up with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:59:44-07:00","id":1561295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561293#post1561293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the FTL method used. Wormholes for example wouldn't be able to create kinetic planet killer weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural forming wormholes would also be restricted to pre-set destinations. Severely limiting their practicality, unless we invented a method for creating our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T06:25:59-07:00","id":1561296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561294#post1561294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was just checking, because I remember something about them creating a law where Tibetan monks needed the government's permission to reincarnate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which, hilariously, sounds like something the Celestial Bureaucracy might come up with!</div> </div> </div> </div>In some respects, but here it's just to the practical point of the CCP yoking control of the two lama system, where the Dalai Lama recognizes the reincarnation of the Panchen Lama, and vice versa. Saying that the government requires permission for reincarnation means that the CCP gets to de facto identify which is which and basically co-opts Tibet for them. Hence the Dalai Lama declaring that he just won't reincarnate, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:23:22-07:00","id":1561304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561282#post1561282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is that we're following Shadowrun Rules, where the power of magic is cyclical in nature; waxing in one age, and waning in the next.<br /> <br /> But if that is the case, then it doesn't account for how the traditions are still able to perform their feats.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's but ONE alternative. We simply don't know.<br /> <br /> And it ignores the difference between reality laws and Awakened Magic.<br /> <br /> Mages can reshape reality, period. Existence of actual natural laws is not a factor. Be it natural or just the Consensus, Gravity is real, yet any Mage can magically nullify it because that's what Mages do.<br /> <br /> It does mean, though, that Sleepers need to find ways around it that Mages don't need. And that's what a lot of flying systems Mages had no hand in developing do.<br /> <br /> We're talking two co-ocurring but distinct phenomena that, while the Consensus Theory covers both, are not necessarily linked: the <b><i>Age of Reason</i></b> and the <i><b>Rise of Paradox</b></i>.<br /> <br /> On the <b>Age of Reason</b>, this is about &quot;natural&quot; laws indeed. It's about how easily Sleepers can develop their own magics, if this world is apt to house creatures like dragons, and many other things <i>that exist without any Mage nearby</i>. And while this shrunk considerably, overall there's still a lot of lower case magic and wonder in the WoD, and no confirmation that the trend is permanent. In fact M20 does leave in the air the possibility it is already starting to reverse.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b> is a problem that started way back when, since the first confirmed change was the very reason for House Tremere to do what they did, about a thousand years ago. And it took several weird forms, <i><b>they don't really fit the theory very well, not even now</b></i>.<br /> <br /> While the last confirmed change by the end of the 90s just made it stronger, previous iterations like the <b>Scourge</b> simply didn't work at all the way <b>Paradox</b> does. And even today it poses an unanswered question: if it is reality trying to preserve the Consensus, <i>why the fuck is it even weirder than its cause</i>? Many answers have been proposed, but the very idea that it is Consensus' defense doesn't actually have strong evidence to begin with.<br /> <br /> Similarly to the last, though, we just never reached the worst possible situation, if we're even right about it. The world is most definitely still a magical place, and a lot of the dullness that in the 90s we thought to be antithetical to magic simply isn't. You totally can be Magical and boring at the same time.<br /> <br /> Yet the actual evidence <u><b>never</b></u> showed Magic to become harder to do, just to develop weirder consequences. The effects that became really hard to maintain indefinitely are very specific, and the difficulty to perform Magic <u>is exactly the same as always</u>. What increased \u2013 Paradox and Backlash \u2013 are <i><b>the increasingly bizarre collateral results of careless Magic</b></i>.<br /> <br /> So, the setting doesn't actually look anything like Shadowrun's cyclic magic even IF it runs on some cyclic system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561282#post1561282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already saw another discussion about this kind of stuff in a different thread, where the argument was about how all the different splats clash with and contradict each other.<br /> <br /> For the sake of convenience, I'm going with the assumption that as this is a mage related thread, we are only using mage related subject matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it would be nonsensical to do otherwise.<br /> <br /> But Mage doesn't assume reality is uniquely shaped by Mages. The game has extensive discussions on what kinds of other entities exist out there, especially in the Umbra, how reality may actually work and which role such entities may have in it.<br /> <br /> There's zero need to step out of Mage to think the causes of the Age of Reason and the Rise of Paradox may lay elsewhere. Mage alone has Nightfolk, Bygones, Animistic Spirits, Ghosts, Abstract Spirits, Avatars, Gods, Angels, Demons, Other Dimensions, Other Timelines, Realms, Zones, Dream Realms, Paths of Weird, Astral Umbra with Vulgate, Spires and Epiphanies, Djinn as an independent intelligent race, Dark Umbra, several experiences of the Penumbra that may or may not be three distinct but related realities, and several still unclassified entities and events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561282#post1561282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, however...<br /> <br /> 1 - Technocrats are mages, regardless of how much they deny it.<br /> <br /> 2 - Technocrats have spent centuries shaping the Sleeper's perception of reality, and by extension shaping Consensus.<br /> <br /> The fact they eventually lost control of the situation does not change the fact that the world as we currently understand it today was shaped by the Technocracy manipulating our world view.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy <i>trying</i> to manipulate and shape the Sleeper's perception of reality, based on a <i>theory</i> of Consensus, is a fact.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy <i>being the actual cause</i> of the current state vs just getting lucky <u><b>is not</b></u>, this is a <i>conjecture</i> that seemed safe at first, <i>but has several holes</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561282#post1561282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess you haven't heard of the <i>&quot;Let it Rot&quot;</i> movement, where China's youth are opting out of the work environment, and deliberately allowing the country to collapse around them?<br /> <br /> Also, didn't the CCP enforce atheism on a national level?</div> </div> </div> </div>What any of that has to do with anything? The point is that the Consensus, if real, would not be shaped by US suburban culture, or any US culture at all.<br /> <br /> And for the game the failure by the CCP at promoting atheism is way more relevant, and a demonstration of Technocratic failure.<br /> <br /> They don't do that anymore, anyway, haven't for a very long time. They do control authorization for religions, though, for pragmatic reasons we can discuss all day if they're good or bad, well thought or stupid, but are still pragmatic in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:28:00-07:00","id":1561305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561293#post1561293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the FTL method used. Wormholes for example wouldn't be able to create kinetic planet killer weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said FTL ships specifically when talking about how technology always comes with the risk of being put to harmful uses.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> As for the CCP: the current government recognizes five legal religions which are allowed to be publicly practiced, and huge amount of folk religion that as noted they just gave up trying to get rid of as long as people keep it private.<br /> <br /> The government considers itself atheist, but that's not really any different from most Western democracies considering themselves secular: there's no state religion and the government is supposed to not promote specific religions. What they don't have is a pluralist approach of religions freedom and tolerance; so even with legal religion religions can still be discriminated against in public life (such as denying openly religious people positions in government and agencies/military service).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:47:56-07:00","id":1561310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561304#post1561304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy <i>trying</i> to manipulate and shape the Sleeper's perception of reality, based on a <i>theory</i> of Consensus, is a fact.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy <i>being the actual cause</i> of the current state vs just getting lucky <u><b>is not</b></u>, this is a <i>conjecture</i> that seemed safe at first, <i>but has several holes</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes the setting more depressing.<br /> <br /> Because IF the rise of Paradox was, indeed, caused by shifting consensus, then that means it can theoretically be fixed if any of the Traditions managed to get the upper hand.<br /> <br /> However, if the rise of Paradox is just a natural occurrence that happened on its own, then that makes it sound like the universe itself just spontaneously decided <i>&quot;lol, magic is stupid!&quot;</i> and there's nothing we can do about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:56:34-07:00","id":1561313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561310#post1561310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, if the rise of Paradox is just a natural occurrence that happened on its own<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a false dichotomy. Actually, two:<br /> <br /> 1. Not being caused by the Technocracy does not means the cause is natural, and even if it is, does not means there's nothing we can do.<br /> <br /> 2. I'll point again that evidence shows that Magic is still easy as ever, casting just became weirder, and the world is still plenty magical. On top of that, things can improve even on their own, as M20 transpires it may already be happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T13:40:21-07:00","id":1561316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561304#post1561304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet the actual evidence <u><b>never</b></u> showed Magic to become harder to do, just to develop weirder consequences. The effects that became really hard to maintain indefinitely are very specific, and the difficulty to perform Magic <u>is exactly the same as always</u>. What increased \u2013 Paradox and Backlash \u2013 are <i><b>the increasingly bizarre collateral results of careless Magic</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that that's true. Mages in the Dark Ages had bigger dice pools and weren't as difficulty effected by whether or not something should be possible, weren't they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T14:35:00-07:00","id":1561319,"title":"","content":"DA Mage let you get dice-pools up faster, but the final end-points are pretty much the same; so learning magic was - at least by the mechanics - much easier/faster but not necessarily less difficult to do. DA Mage also let you buy Pillars higher than your Foundations which added to potential difficulties as those mages could learn magic before they had the self-mastery to apply smoothly. Learning faster didn't make magic easier, but generally harder as it opened mages up to more avenues of hubris.<br /> <br /> It also shifted who decides &quot;whether or not something should be possible.&quot; In DA, the mage themselves is the most potent source of that. The Foundation/Pillar system means mages have whole effects they couldn't learn without the intense and arduous process of learning Pillars from other Fellowships because that's what it would take to expand their personal ideas of possible beyond their starting Pillars conceptualizations of what magic can do. <br /> <br /> During the Sorcerer's Crusade (and I feel it's worth noting that the Order of Reason and the Technocracy have been conflated a lot in this discussion, but there are meaningful differences between them esp. regarding their views on what Consensus even is and what to do with it), Reality Zones became the dominant factor of what counts as possible. This very much lays the groundwork for the Ascension War because the Order of Reason couldn't really execute its desires in light of how much power this gave to the newly formed Traditions. Most of the Traditions came out of regional groups which meant they had immense home court advantage when in friendly Reality Zones. The want to homogenize humanity to break down the Reality Zones and make the Traditions less able to dig in and endure lead to the eventual restructuring of the OoR into the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It's only after European colonialism (and esp. the sun never slept on the British Empire) largely succeeded in forcing most of the globe into a more shared reality with the Technocracy's aid that humanity as a whole started becoming the primary arbiter of possible. But even then Reality Zones are just reduced, not fully eliminated. <br /> <br /> Those shifts in who the primary determiner of &quot;possible&quot; was also follows the trends in what happened if you violated possibility. DA resulted in a very clear, &quot;I must have screwed up and now magical energy is wrecking myself or my stuff,&quot; as it was more personal. In SC scourging followed the logic of the local Reality Zones. Modern times as phrased above... things just got weirder because things got more abstract from so many individuals giving &quot;feedback&quot; at once.<br /> <br /> This is also mirrored in other parts of the setting's metaphysics. In DA mages didn't even know about Avatars because Avatars were so seamlessly merged to the mages that there was no perception of them as a separate being; also leading to a lot of confusing them for souls or similar concepts. In SC Avatars start to become distinct but still fairly consistent in manifestations by local standards. By the modern era Avatars are weird with little rhyme or reason to the vast variety in ways they appear to their mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T15:24:02-07:00","id":1561321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561316#post1561316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that that's true. Mages in the Dark Ages had bigger dice pools and weren't as difficulty effected by whether or not something should be possible, weren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Heavy Arms said, in the end the dice pool size was basically the same, just easier to start higher. And what changed most wasn't how hard it is to cast what should be impossible, but how possibility is even defined.<br /> <br /> Difficulty itself remained quite constant. Let's just remember, to begin with, that Mages have several ways to reduce Diff up to -3 from initial, enough that you can assume it as the default for any Magic done without rushing. So Vulgar With Witness is actually Sphere +2, to a max of Diff 7. This is not a terribly hard feat for a Mage with Arete 6 or 7, and is for the most egregious violations against reality, otherwise it's easier.<br /> <br /> No Paradox will ever stop you from doing that. It may hurt you for doing so, but never stop. In fact, the backlash is likely to just add to total weirdness level. You can transmute a trashcan into a multi-localized Bat-Polar Bear with magnetic breath in broad daylight in front of everyone, and instead of stopping you, Paradox will add Pennywise to the scene. That's Mage in Revised, the most severe Paradox rule in the history of the game.<br /> <br /> Of course, other things will happen to clean up this mess, but they overall boil down to other people working on it. Even Unmaking isn't any reality defense, it's Sleepers exerting their Will in the basic but very real way they can - it's them Magicking away your Magic.<br /> <br /> What's worse/better in all this is that we don't really know why Paradox took the form it took each time, or which better represent its real nature, if there's any. The Traditions and the Technocracy have theories, but they're that: theories. And they're complicated by the nature of Awakening: you can't test things because your belief alters the result.<br /> <br /> You're the worst nightmare of science: a field of unfalsifiability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T00:37:15-07:00","id":1561373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559726-a-problem-with-mage?p=1561316#post1561316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that that's true. Mages in the Dark Ages had bigger dice pools and weren't as difficulty effected by whether or not something should be possible, weren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Ages was when magic <b>started to</b> malfunction, so the effects weren't quite as severe as they would later become in modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}